Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
-2x - 4 & \text{if } x \le 2, \\
\frac{x}{3} + 2 & \text{if } x > 2.
\end{array}
\right.\] Find the sum of all values of $x$ such that $f(x) = 0$.

What is the value of $x$ if \begin{align*}
x &= y + 8, \\
y &= z + 15, \\
z &= w + 25, \\
\text{and }\qquad w &= 90 ?
\end{align*}

In the following diagram, $AB=60$. Given that $C$ is a point on line segment $AB$ such that $AC = 40$ and $BC = 20$, find $AX$.

[asy]
import markers;

real t=.67;
pair A=(0,0);
pair B=(3,-2);
pair C=(1.5,1.5);
pair X=t*A+(1-t)*B;

draw(C--A--B--C--X);

label("$A$",A,SW);
label("$B$",B,E);
label("$C$",C,N);
label("$X$",X,SW);

markangle(n=1,radius=15,A,C,X,marker(markinterval(stickframe(n=1),true)));
markangle(n=1,radius=15,X,C,B,marker(markinterval(stickframe(n=1),true)));

label("40",.5*(B+C),E);
label("20",.5*(A+C),NW);
[/asy]

Given the function $f(x)=ae^{x}+bx\ln x$, the equation of the tangent line at $x=1$ is $y=2ex-e$.  
(Ⅰ) Find the values of the real numbers $a$ and $b$;  
(Ⅱ) Find the minimum value of the function $g(x)=f(x)-ex^{2}$.

In the diagram below, $AB = AC = 130,$ $AD = 50,$ and $CF = 50.$ Compute $\frac{[CEF]}{[DBE]}.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.025 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F;

B = (0,0);
C = (100,0);
A = intersectionpoint(arc(B,130,0,180),arc(C,130,0,180));
D = interp(A,B,50/130);
F = interp(A,C,130/180);
E = extension(B,C,D,F);

draw(C--B--A--F--D);

label("$A$", A, N);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, NE);
